.TH SDL_HINT_MOUSE_EMULATE_WARP_WITH_RELATIVE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MOUSE_EMULATE_WARP_WITH_RELATIVE \- A variable controlling whether warping a hidden mouse cursor will activate relative mouse mode.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MOUSE_EMULATE_WARP_WITH_RELATIVE \(dqSDL_MOUSE_EMULATE_WARP_WITH_RELATIVE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
When this hint is set, the mouse cursor is hidden, and multiple warps to the window center occur within a short time period, SDL will emulate mouse warps using relative mouse mode\[char46] This can provide smoother and more reliable mouse motion for some older games, which continuously calculate the distance traveled by the mouse pointer and warp it back to the center of the window, rather than using relative mouse motion\[char46]
.PP
Note that relative mouse mode may have different mouse acceleration behavior than pointer warps\[char46]
.PP
If your application needs to repeatedly warp the hidden mouse cursor at a high-frequency for other purposes, it should disable this hint\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Attempts to warp the mouse will always be made\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Some mouse warps will be emulated by forcing relative mouse mode\[char46] (default)
.PP
If not set, this is automatically enabled unless an application uses relative mouse mode directly\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

